+# Evidence Contract: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Project ID**: `001-pulseboard`
+**Project Archetype**: b2b_saas
+**Play Level**: build
+**Speck Version**: 10.5.0
+**Last Updated**: 2026-08-11
+
+## 0. Governing proof rules
+
+This contract proves runtime behavior, not intent. A gate begins by trying to falsify a claim; a claim needs an observed mechanism; unreachable flows are defects; and an independently motivated evaluator judges the evidence. Tests establish correctness only. They cannot establish production delivery, workspace isolation, or experience quality without the runtime evidence named below.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web | Versioned production web bundle served from the release configuration | Production web deployment |
+
+Assumption: the repository declares no native, desktop, CLI, or API-only target. Adding one requires a platform-specific amendment before it can claim readiness.
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Web
+
+- A clean production build, served by the release-equivalent server; the build SHA and sanitized configuration are recorded.
+- A browser recording, screenshots, accessibility tree, and browser console/network record from that build for each required LARP flow.
+- A real authenticated request as each named workspace principal, including both permitted and forbidden reads against the deployed authorization layer.
+- A pre-walk datastore baseline plus a post-walk read-back proving a confirmed reminder was written once, scheduled once, and has one terminal delivery record.
+- A real delivery-provider result or an observed terminal failure persisted to the reminder record; no client-side success indication may substitute for it.
+
+### Claim-to-instrument admissibility
+
+| Claim type | Admissible evidence | Does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Correctness | Tests, static checks, or live probes | A screenshot alone |
+| Workspace visibility | Live permitted and forbidden reads as real workspace principals | Mocked clients, service-role reads, or endpoint 404s |
+| Delivery acceptance | Provider/deployed-boundary response and persisted outcome | A mocked provider response |
+| Persistence / exactly once | Baseline and datastore read-back keyed to one reminder | UI success state or an unbaselined post-read |
+| Reachability and fit | Built-browser walk, accessibility tree, and measured layout at three widths | Source assertions, jsdom geometry, or unjudged captures |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+- Development-server, Storybook-only, or localhost captures for UX-RC, SHIP-RC, or SHIP claims.
+- Mock auth or service-role access cited for workspace-isolation claims.
+- Mock delivery, client timers, or a UI "sent" label cited for exactly-once delivery.
+- A post-delivery read without a pre-delivery baseline, because an old row can look like new delivery.
+- Unadjudicated screenshots, passing tests, or static scans cited as evidence of product quality or production behavior.
+- A stale build, a cached build not compiled from the validated SHA, hidden/skipped tests, tautological assertions, or evaluator-authored gate changes in the graded implementation change.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP
+
+### UX-RC
+
+| Persona | Primary flow | Required falsification evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Team facilitator | Draft action → inspect text, owner, due date → explicitly confirm → view scheduled reminder | Recording plus read-back; attempt to schedule before confirmation must be refused and logged |
+| Member of workspace A | Sign in → view A's transcript/actions/delivery status | Live permitted read as A; attempt to read workspace B must return no data and leave no side effect |
+| Reminder recipient | Receive a confirmed reminder → inspect delivery state | Delivery-provider result or truthful persisted terminal failure; retry/reload must not create a second delivery |
+| Second actor on same browser profile | A creates data → sign out → B signs in | B sees no A data in server data, browser storage, queue, draft, or delivery status |
+
+At UX-RC each flow has a functional DOES-IT-WORK record and an independent IS-IT-GOOD critique of every material screen. At SHIP-RC, repeat the flows against the launch build with real authorization and delivery integration.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Functional completion only makes a flow eligible for judgment. The evaluator records separate 0–10 scores for correctness, on-contract behavior, felt-good legibility, trust, and commercial clarity. A score above 8 requires distinct pixel- or interaction-grounded criticism and no active P0/P1; an active P0/P1 caps the affected dimension at 4. Reusing a critique across dimensions caps those dimensions at 8.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+For UX-RC or higher, store the build SHA, build command, sanitized configuration, LARP recording, screenshots, accessibility tree, console/network log, and datastore/provider read-backs. A browser-delivered secret scan must cover every emitted asset and prerendered HTML/payload surface used by the chosen web framework.
+
+### 6a. CI-Enforced Gate Registry
+
+| Gate ID | Command / Script | Stage | Domain | Scope | Subject | Canary | Waiver |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| speck:evidence-contract | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-contract.sh --strict` | manual | evidence contract | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence-contract.md` | `files>0` | exempt:documentation-only | — |
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | typed evidence citations | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/**` | `citations>0` once runtime evidence exists | — | — |
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+No external service, database, authentication provider, or delivery provider is named in the current project truth. This is not proof that none will exist. Before a component can claim INTEGRATION-GREEN, it must be added here with a live round-trip proof and an anti-proof rule.
+
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+
+No public profile surface is declared in the workspace. If a README, landing page, package listing, or deployment URL is added, SHIP-RC requires an evidence-backed check that its product claim matches the three promises in `product-contract.md` and does not overstate readiness.
+
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence |
+|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Default until all later gates have their required runtime evidence. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Tests, lint, types, and clean build pass; evaluator isolation and no hidden/skipped or tautological tests are checked. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | IMPL-GREEN plus real auth, persistence, and delivery round trips for every integrated service; baseline/read-back confirms the write path. |
+| UX-RC | INTEGRATION-GREEN plus all §4 persona flows on a clean production build, including independent functional and experiential judgments. |
+| API-RC | Not applicable unless an API-only surface is introduced; then use deployed contract and stress-test evidence. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | Not applicable until a paid path is declared; then real sandbox purchase, entitlement, restore, failure, and webhook evidence are mandatory. |
+| SHIP-RC | UX-RC plus launch-build replay of all promise probes, no unresolved P0/P1, fresh evidence, and PROFILE alignment. |
+| SHIP | Human release decision after SHIP-RC plus post-deploy smoke evidence from the released build. |
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage Paths
+
+| Evidence | Canonical path |
+|---|---|
+| Persona scripts | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/personas/<persona-id>.md` |
+| Screenshots and browser artifacts | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/screenshots/` |
+| LARP recordings, AX trees, logs, and probe outputs | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/larp-recordings/` |
+| Validation verdict and typed citations | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/validation-report.md` |
+
+## 10. Freshness and surrogate-proof policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when its build SHA is the validated commit or its source behavior has not changed since collection; evidence older than 14 days is stale. Anti-proof may be recorded as a diagnostic, but it must be labeled surrogate proof and cannot support UX-RC or higher.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Probe | Failure-path attempt | Required behavior |
+|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001 incomplete confirmation | Omit action text, owner, or due date; attempt schedule by UI and direct request | Refuse scheduling; no reminder, queue entry, or provider call is created |
+| PRM-001 tampered confirmation | Change any confirmed field before schedule submission | Confirmation is invalidated and requires a new explicit confirmation |
+| PRM-002 cross-workspace read | A requests B's transcript, action, and delivery-status identifiers | No data is returned; no status distinction leaks; request is audit-logged without content |
+| PRM-002 second-actor residue | A writes, signs out, then B uses the same browser offline and online | B cannot read A's data from server, cache, draft, queue, or delivery state |
+| PRM-003 duplicate delivery | Replay the same confirmed reminder concurrently and retry after ambiguous provider timeout | At most one provider delivery is accepted; duplicate attempts are idempotently recorded |
+| PRM-003 provider failure | Force provider rejection, timeout, and unavailable response | A persisted truthful terminal failure is visible; no false "delivered" state appears |
+| Malformed or missing authorization | Missing, malformed, expired, and wrong-workspace credentials | Stable refusal; never 500 or cross-workspace data |
+| Concurrent update | Two actors alter the same action/reminder | Defined conflict outcome with audit trail; never silent loss or duplicate schedule |
+| Oversized/malformed payload | Submit invalid or oversized action/reminder content | Stable 4xx refusal; never provider call, partial write, or 500 |
+| Delivery rate limit | Exceed delivery attempt threshold | Retryable failure is explicit and no duplicate delivery is emitted |
+| Data deletion | Delete a workspace/member and query related reminder records | Related data is removed or anonymized according to the implemented policy; read-back proves it |
+| Comprehension | Cold-start the facilitator flow | A first-time evaluator identifies confirmation as the final scheduling action and can find it without instructions |
+
+## 11a. Standard Probe Library
+
+| Probe ID | Class | Claim type | Admissible substrate | Required negative controls | Discharge artifact | Exception |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PROBE:provenance | P1 | `behaviour` | render site + generator stamp + the prompt's own exemplars, judged control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt with the shipped model | rendered-with-degraded-provenance · exemplar re-read (deleting the exemplar must not leave the test green) | — | n/a:no generative surface is declared |
+| PROBE:honest-label | P2 | `persistence` | the write's observed outcome read back out of the datastore against a pre-walk baseline | total-failure render · partial-failure render · the three renders differ | — | n/a:no delivery implementation exists yet |
+| PROBE:second-actor | P3 | `visibility` | A writes, teardown, B signs in on the same install, offline — once per enumerated persistence layer | signOut vs deleteAccount compared field-for-field · launch-with-data-and-no-owner-record | — | n/a:no persistence implementation exists yet |
+| PROBE:money-path | P4 | `acceptance` | the real engine as the applying principal, one run per revenue path | entitlement gate flipped and every revenue path goes red · vendor fixture cited to the vendor's field reference · per-user serialized claim write · one declared fail-posture · bounded worst case per tap | — | n/a:no revenue path is declared |
+| PROBE:named-clock | P5 | `correctness` | an AST/lint rule over write handlers, cache fills and fixtures, plus the date-sensitive suites run under two timezones | a non-UTC TZ run · allowlist entries that name the audience | — | n/a:no scheduling implementation exists yet |
+| PROBE:geometry-ax | P6 | `fit` | a baked build: platform AX dump plus container-vs-content geometry at 3 or more widths, numbers in the artifact | adjacent-target overlap · expected-cell presence · page overflow | — | n/a:no UI implementation exists yet |
+| PROBE:substrate | P7 | `correctness` | §2b parity of this contract against Speck's compiled admissibility table | the parity run reports CITATION_TABLE_PARITY over a non-empty row set | — | n/a:no runtime citations exist yet |
+| PROBE:migration-dirt | P8 | `acceptance` | the migration applied forward on a throwaway seeded to the target's real dirty shape | pre-state REJECTED · boundary cases still refuse · one migration head after the merge | — | n/a:no datastore or migrations are declared |
+
+The exceptions above document absent surfaces only; they do not discharge an implemented surface. The matching row must be converted to a typed, admissible runtime citation before its feature may advance beyond IMPL-GREEN.
